# FTHR Clips — ignore rules
#
# Rule of thumb: source, build scripts, project files and licence texts are
# tracked. Anything a build regenerates, anything a user produces at runtime,
# and anything we can re-download from a pinned manifest is not.
#
# If you add a rule here, check `git status --ignored` afterwards and make sure
# you did not accidentally shadow a real source file. `.gitignore` has bitten
# this project once already (`AppDir/` used to swallow the .desktop source).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party binaries — re-downloadable, verified by sha256
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The FFmpeg *headers* and *import libs* under third_party/ffmpeg/{include,lib}
# ARE tracked: without them the Windows engine cannot compile at all, and they
# are small. Only the runtime DLLs / .exe (152 MB) are excluded — fetch them
# with `python tools/fetch_third_party.py --ffmpeg`, which verifies the sha256
# recorded in tools/ffmpeg_manifest.json.
FTHRcapture/FTHRclips/third_party/ffmpeg/bin/

# Linux: the pinned LGPL FFmpeg the engine is built against and ships with
# (AUDIT-014). ~57 MB of headers and libraries, fetched and sha256-verified by
# `python tools/fetch_third_party.py --ffmpeg-linux`. Unlike the Windows side
# nothing here is tracked: headers and libs must come from the same archive, so
# splitting them would let them drift apart.
FTHRcapture_linux/third_party/

# MSVC redistributable pulled in by the Inno Setup installer.
# Fetch with `python tools/fetch_third_party.py --vcredist`.
redist/

